    "ㄺ": "Usually only the ㄱ is heard at the end. Before a vowel both sound: ㄹ stays and ㄱ carries over. A plain ㄱ ㄷ ㅂ ㅅ ㅈ right after it turns tense (ㄲ ㄸ ㅃ ㅆ ㅉ).",
    "ㄻ": "Only the ㅁ is heard at the end. Before a vowel both sound: ㄹ stays and ㅁ carries over. At the end of a verb stem, a ㄷ right after it turns tense (ㄸ).",
    "ㄼ": "Usually only the ㄹ is heard at the end. Before a vowel both sound: ㄹ stays and ㅂ carries over. At the end of a verb stem, a ㄷ right after it turns tense (ㄸ).",
    "ㅀ": "Sounds like ㄹ. Before a vowel the ㅎ drops out; before ㄷ it makes ㅌ.",
    "ㅄ": "Only the ㅂ is heard at the end. Before a vowel the ㅅ carries over as a tense ㅆ. A plain ㄱ ㄷ ㅂ ㅅ ㅈ right after it turns tense (ㄲ ㄸ ㅃ ㅆ ㅉ).",
    "ㄷ ㅌ ㄸ": "Plain ㄷ is soft, ㅌ comes with a puff of air, and ㄸ is tight with no air at all.",
